DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssnnmmppdd__mmeettrriiccss exports the following (partial) MIBs via an AgentX compati‐
     ble (snmp) daemon: HOST-RESOURCES-MIB, IF-MIB, OPENBSD-PF-MIB, OPENBSD-
     SENSORS-MIB, OPENBSD-CARP-MIB, OPENBSD-MEM-MIB, IP-MIB, IP-FORWARD-MIB,
     UCD-DISKIO-MIB, and BRIDGE-MIB.

     The options are as follows:

     --CC _o_p_t_i_o_n
             Enable MIB-specific options.  Currently only ffiilltteerr--rroouutteess is
             supported.  If set ask the kernel to filter route update messages
             on the routing socket.  Routing table information will not be
             available, but CPU use will be reduced during bulk updates.

     --cc _c_o_n_t_e_x_t
             The SNMPv3 context and can usually be omitted.

     --dd      Do not daemonize and log to _s_t_d_e_r_r.

     --ss _p_a_t_h
             Connect to the AgentX master via _p_a_t_h.  It defaults to
             _/_v_a_r_/_a_g_e_n_t_x_/_m_a_s_t_e_r.

     --vv      Produce more verbose output.

